"Assigns performing, accountable, consulting and informed roles to specific activities or deliverables.\n\nUse when: Resolve unclear ownership across a shared process. Agree who must participate before and after a decision.\n\nAvoid when: The main need is a reporting hierarchy or the timing of task dependencies.\n\nVisual grammar: Rows identify activities or deliverables; columns identify roles. Cells use a defined R, A, C or I convention. A short legend explains combined assignments and any local policy.\n\nBuild: Choose bounded activities with concrete completion conditions. Identify performing roles and the authority accountable for each result. Agree consultation and notification needs with the affected roles.\n\nCheck: Every activity has sufficient responsibility and a clear accountable authority. Assignments are accepted by the roles they constrain. Consulted and informed participation remain meaningfully distinct.\n\nPitfalls: Assigning everyone to consultation and recreating a bottleneck. Using initials without agreeing what each letter permits or requires.\n\nExample: A community event assigns volunteer scheduling to the coordinator, final approval to the event lead and consultation to venue staff.\n\nAlternatives: Organization chart, Swimlane flowchart."
